/*! @brief querystring module provides some utility functions for parsing and serializing URL query parameters, using the querystring module can easily parse URL query parameters into objects or strings, and can also serialize objects into URL query parameter strings

The following are the commonly used functions of the `querystring` module:

- `querystring.parse(str[, sep[, eq[, options]]])`: Parse URL query parameters into an object
- `querystring.stringify(obj[, sep[, eq[, options]]])`: Serialize an object into a URL query parameter string

Among them, `str` is the URL query parameter string to be parsed, `obj` is the object to be serialized.

The following example illustrates how to use the `querystring` module to parse query parameters from a URL into an object:

```JavaScript
const querystring = require('querystring');

const url = 'https://www.example.com/path/to/page?foo=bar&baz=qux';

const search = new URL(url).search; // return '?foo=bar&baz=qux'
const query = querystring.parse(search.slice(1)); // parse query string

console.log(query); // output { foo: 'bar', baz: 'qux' }
```

The above code first gets a URL, then extracts the query parameter part from it, uses the `querystring.parse()` function to parse it into an object, and finally prints the object.

Next, the example illustrates how to use the `querystring` module to serialize an object into a URL query parameter string:

```JavaScript
const querystring = require('querystring');

const obj = {
  foo: 'bar',
  baz: 'qux'
};

const query = querystring.stringify(obj);

console.log(query); // output "foo=bar&baz=qux"
```

In the above code, an object is first defined, then the `querystring.stringify()` function is used to serialize it into a URL query parameter string, and finally the string is printed.

It can be found that using the `querystring` module can conveniently parse and serialize URL query parameters, reduce the tedious processing of strings, and improve the readability and maintainability of the code.
 */
module querystring
{
    /*! @brief url component string safe encoding
     @param str url to encode
     @return Return the encoded string
     */
    static String escape(String str);

    /*! @brief url safe string decoding
     @param str url to decode
     @return Return the decoded string
     */
    static String unescape(String str);

    /*! @brief Parse query string
     @param str String to parse
     @param sep Separator string used for parsing, default is &
     @param eq Assignment string used for parsing, default is =
     @param opt Parsing parameters, not supported yet
     @return Return the decoded object
     */
    static HttpCollection parse(String str, String sep = "&", String eq = "=", Object opt = {});

    /*! @brief Serialize an object to query string
     @param obj Object to serialize
     @param sep Separator string used for serialization, default is &
     @param eq Assignment string used for serialization, default is =
     @param opt Parsing parameters, not supported yet
     @return Return the serialized string
     */
    static String stringify(Object obj, String sep = "&", String eq = "=", Object opt = {});
};